{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"normalized Laplacian spectrum. nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kemeny_constant"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kemenyConstant"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vol · (Σᵢ πᵢ (L_g⁻¹)ᵢᵢ − πᵀ L_g⁻¹ π), π the stationary distribution, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1\/2vol) Σᵢⱼ dᵢ dⱼ R(i, j) (commute times are vol · R), with L_g the Laplacian grounded at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex of largest degree and eliminated as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"type":"text","text":". Every term is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sum of positive ones and the difference loses at most a factor n, so the result keeps its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE14kemenyConstant6weightSdSgqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_tSBRd__lF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kemenyConstant","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","precise